Restore the original empty polygon-list terminator in Highlight_Area.

Original dd2h.exe @43b704 reads byte 43a7b0 (ff); @43b70c stores it
at ebp-4 before selecting the triangle/quad highlight index lists.
Areas 1, 3, 6, 8 and 9 use this local empty list for one polygon
type. Ghidra omitted the initialization because its source lies in
the executable text section. The port instead traversed uninitialized
stack bytes as signed polygon indices, overwriting model vertices,
polygon headers and indices when the pit camera highlighted the car.
The recorded regular championship race reaches this path at cf10605:
native corrupts geometry and intermittently crashes in face handlers;
browser WASM traps in FUN_0041ff98's indirect polygon dispatch.
Restore only the literal original terminator; keep all original list
selection, signed indexing, RGB writes and polygon traversal intact.

